---
title: Quick Calamari with Garlic Mayonnaise
servings: 4
course: Starter
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
---

> Double quantities to serve as a main course.

= Garlic Mayonnaise =

Grate or crush the @garlic{0.5%clove} into the @mayonnaise{100%g} and stir to mix.

= Calamari =

Heat the @groundnut oil{250%ml}(or as needed depending on size of pan) in a smallish saucepan and, while it’s left to warm up, cut the thawed @frozen squid, tubes and tentacles{500%g} into 1 cm rings.

Put the @cornflour{2%tbsp}, @semolina{4%tbsp}, @salt{1%tsp}, and @paprika{1%tsp} into a plastic freezer bag.

Add the squid rings and tentacles and then toss to coat.

When the oil is hot enough, which is when it sizzles up fiercely when you drop in a small cube of bread, fry the squid in batches to get the most golden crunchiness. A couple of minutes per batch is all you should need.